{"title":"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#First_Hint\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">First Hint</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Second_Hint\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Second Hint</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Final_Hint\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Final Hint</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a25c2f9720d16d7ab307b6766d3539fad0a05b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" /> is an arbitrary sequence of positive integers. A member of the sequence is picked at \nrandom. Its value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Another member is picked at random, independently of the first. Its value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Then a third value, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Show that the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/545223d83982de1935d74094bcd5f975bc86ce6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b +c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd0f9f9869b39e79527f9010293adf7bfe5210f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"First_Hint\">First Hint</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: First Hint\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The given problem is equivalent to proving that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4ccb4fbf01977f019ac762f383e2eea58584ce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(x^3 + y^3 + z^3 + 6xyz) \\ge (x + y + z)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"297\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Second_Hint\">Second Hint</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Second Hint\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Try proving this inequality for all nonnegative real numbers x, y, z; not just positive integers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Final_Hint\">Final Hint</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Final Hint\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce0770e77b0e1da55b799daf491c79867cc52d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + y^3 + z^3 + 3xyz \\ge x^2(y+z) + y^2(x+z) + z^2(x+y).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"447\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let x equal the probability of picking an element of the sequence equivalent to 0 mod 3, y equal those 1 mod 3, and z equal those 2 mod 3. Then, considering that 0+0+0, 1+1+1, 2+2+2, and 0+1+2 are divisible by 3, we obtain the equivalent inequality in the First Hint. This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a0548981b5a195ef9f469f36d86f0974129b481e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + y^3 + z^3 + 6xyz \\ge x^2(y+z) + y^2(x+z) + z^2(x+y).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"451\" height=\"21\" /> Now, we attempt to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce0770e77b0e1da55b799daf491c79867cc52d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + y^3 + z^3 + 3xyz \\ge x^2(y+z) + y^2(x+z) + z^2(x+y).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"447\" height=\"19\" /> for all nonnegative real numbers x, y, z; our inequality will follow from this. But this is just Schur's Inequality with r = 1! This completes the proof.\n</p><p><i>Note: Schur's Inequality states that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aa11afadb41bd746429ec340a6695ca4793dc0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^r(x-y)(x-z) + y^r(y-z)(y-x) + z^r(z-x)(z-y) \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"463\" height=\"18\" />. This can be proven by setting WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69a3849b6e275e68de33f23398b08eaa079897a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge y \\ge z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and bunching together terms that are nonnegative. Challenge: when does equality hold? When does equality hold in the problem?</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO\" title=\"1979 USAMO\">1979 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1979\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017031301\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.02